<article class="env-lemma" id="07BQ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/07BQ">Lemma <span data-tag="07BQ">10.134.9</span>.</a> Let $R_\lambda \to S_\lambda $ be a system of ring maps over the directed set $\Lambda $. Set $R = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits R_\lambda $ and $S = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits S_\lambda $. Then $\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{S/R} = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits \mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{S_\lambda /R_\lambda }$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Recall that $\mathop{N\! L}\nolimits _{S/R}$ is the complex $I/I^2 \to \bigoplus _{s \in S} S\text{d}[s]$ where $I \subset R[S]$ is the kernel of the canonical presentation $R[S] \to S$. Now it is clear that $R[S] = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits R_\lambda [S_\lambda ]$ and similarly that $I = \mathop{\mathrm{colim}}\nolimits I_\lambda $ where $I_\lambda = \mathop{\mathrm{Ker}}(R_\lambda [S_\lambda ] \to S_\lambda )$. Hence the lemma is clear. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>